      "text": "To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 12 and 20, we can use the Euclidean algorithm. Here are the steps:\n\n1. Divide the larger number (20) by the smaller number (12) and find the remainder:\n   \\[\n   20 \\div 12 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 8\n   \\]\n   So, we can write:\n   \\[\n   20 = 12 \\cdot 1 + 8\n   \\]\n\n2. Now, take the smaller number (12) and divide it by the remainder (8):\n   \\[\n   12 \\div 8 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 4\n   \\]\n   So, we can write:\n   \\[\n   12 = 8 \\cdot 1 + 4\n   \\]\n\n3. Next, take the remainder (4) and divide it by the previous remainder (8):\n   \\[\n   8 \\div 4 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 0\n   \\]\n   So, we can write:\n   \\[\n   8 = 4 \\cdot 2 + 0\n   \\]\n\nSince the remainder is now 0, the GCD is the last non-zero remainder, which is 4.\n\nTherefore, the greatest common divisor of 12 and 20 is \\boxed{4}.",
